-- title:
--   Integral modular function with equal degrees in both characteristics
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and $\Gamma =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image in $\Gamma_0(M)$ of the pullback of $H$ under the character `gamma0Units M`. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid M$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. $\ell$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A`. The assertion is that there is a Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that its coefficientwise image under $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` — the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficient-embedded image of `xHFunctionField M H`, the latter being generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by `intFormRatiosC ℚ Γ` — and its coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal lies in `xHFunctionFieldC k M H`, the subfield of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by `intFormRatiosC k Γ`; moreover the reduction $\bar y$ is transcendental over $k$, the degree of `xHFunctionFieldC k M H` over $k(\bar y)$ is finite and nonzero (stated as $0 <$ `Module.finrank`), and the degree of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(y)$ equals the degree of `xHFunctionFieldC k M H` over $k(\bar y)$.
--
--   This is the Lean form of the comparison, for $\ell \nmid M$, between the degree of the function field of $X_H(M)$ over a line generated by an $\ell$-integral modular function in characteristic $0$ and the degree of the corresponding field of $q$-expansions in characteristic $\ell$, the field-theoretic shadow of Igusa's good reduction of $X_H(M)$ at primes not dividing the level. It is used in the analysis of reduction of places and $q$-expansions at level $\Gamma_H(M)$, in particular by [`ModularCurve.eq_zero_of_reductionQExpModL_gammaH_eq_zero_of_nsmul_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eq_zero_of_reductionQExpModL_gammaH_eq_zero_of_nsmul_eq_zero) and [`ModularCurve.placeReduction_unique_of_forall_mapDomain_eq_ord_gammaH_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.placeReduction_unique_of_forall_mapDomain_eq_ord_gammaH_of_not_dvd).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_transcendental_finrank_adjoin_eq_xHFunctionFieldC_of_not_dvd.lean

import Mathlib
